# J3: TP4 decode benchmark - one stream and 4 / 8 concurrent at 4k to 64k, 4 at 130k (a 131k context), prefill at 130k
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the TP4 bring-up (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env, commit, and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig,
# a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# Duration (estimate, wall clock; the workflow's step limits in parentheses): reset 3-12 min; engine build 20-50 min; bench 45-90 min (11 shapes; every prefill of a shape is serial: 4 x 131k is 4 prefills): about 80-150 min (step 210).
# general-tp4-bench is gate only (8 seats x 131,072, pool 1,048,576 tokens): one engine serves every shape, so the cards open once. The 131k prefill time is the 1x130000 shape ttft. Run J3r for the pair numbers.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-1
C2_PROFILE=general-tp4-bench
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,bench
C2_BENCH_SHAPES=1x4096,1x32768,1x65536,1x130000,4x4096,4x32768,4x65536,8x4096,8x32768,8x65536,4x130000
